Status: IN_PROGRESS - technically verified locally; owner visual review and physical-phone qualification pending.
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/82
Milestone: Movable pear-boy desk lamp with warm diffuse light and expressive physics.
Dependencies: Existing separate-console tabletop; preserve GBA and DS behavior.

Purpose:
Add the owner's pear-character lamp at the desk's upper right with a dedicated
pear lighting dock control, movable body and rope-connected hands and feet.

Tasks:
- [x] Add procedural pear, leaf/stem, face, freckles, hands/feet and warm light.
- [x] Add independent power, 10-100% brightness, movement and reset controls.
- [x] Make braided rope limbs thicker, then lengthen both arms and legs.
- [x] Simulate pinned ropes, inertial swing, body/desk contacts and settling.
- [x] Track the cursor with the eyes; show squeezed eyes and a trembling mouth
      while picked up or falling, with reduced-motion support.
- [x] Support camera-plane dragging, wheel depth, keyboard height, release/drop,
      bounce/friction, workspace bounds, occupied-placement rejection and cancel.
- [x] Broaden warm illumination using distributed emitters; verify near/far
      actual pixels rather than relying only on material/light metadata.
- [x] Verify actual desktop/touch/physics/face interaction and affected darkness.
- [ ] Obtain owner visual review; qualify performance on a physical phone.

Acceptance criteria:
The pear lamp is visible at the upper right, can be moved through the bounded
three-dimensional workspace and dropped with visible gravity/bounce. Longer,
thick rope limbs stay attached and swing. His eyes follow mouse/pen movement
and the scared face lasts through pickup/falling. Lighting controls work
independently, and the light spreads across the surrounding desk. Preserve
full-resolution rendering, the separate consoles and unrelated pending work.

Completion evidence:
One focused Edge gate passes8cases in1.4m: all5pear cases and3affected original
lamp/dark-room/LCD-spill cases. Includes actual near/far illumination pixels,
held movement repaint, real390px touch drag/first dock tap, rope constraints,
face pixels and sampled falling/bounce/settling.32units,syntax and build pass.
Actual local table/scared/airborne captures reviewed; retained figures in
docs/images/pear-boy-table.png and pear-boy-scared.png. Not a full-suite result,
physical-phone qualification, owner approval, push or deployment.
Body remains upright with box-based prop collisions. Ropes collide with the
pear and desk only; arbitrary prop surfaces/moving supports are not simulated.

Completion log:
2026-11-06: Owner requests pear-boy, dock lighting, rope limbs and thicker cords,
then cursor-following/scared expression and free3Dlift/drop. Broaden warm light
after the owner's diffusion feedback. Subsequently lengthen arms and legs,
retaining rope thickness and physics. Fix inter-step anchor stretching and
strengthen bounded constraint convergence after a real browser failure.
Keep this feature local and commit incrementally as Zanark; no publication.
